{%- comment -%}
  Single source of truth for which of the 4 shop-menu categories
  (Clutches, Accessories, Mini Bags, Fits A Phone) each product belongs
  to. Unlike pm-family-data (keyword matching against product.title),
  this is an EXACT product-title lookup -- several products share a
  common prefix but land in different categories (e.g. "Clutch Edge -
  Short" is Clutches but "Clutch Edge - Airpod" is Accessories), so
  keyword matching would misclassify them. Every surface that filters
  by category (desktop Shop menu, mobile Shop panel, the collection
  grid's own filtering) should pull from this rather than keeping its
  own copy.

  Rendered, not included, for the same reason as pm-family-data (some
  shops disable the include tag outright). Callers capture the output
  and split it themselves:

    {%- capture pm_categories_raw -%}{% render 'pm-category-data' %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign pm_categories = pm_categories_raw | strip | split: ';;' -%}

  Format per entry: Exact product title|category handle. Match by
  comparing product.title (stripped, downcased) against the title half
  (also stripped, downcased) -- not a contains/keyword match. A
  product not listed here simply has no category and won't appear
  under any category filter.
{%- endcomment -%}
